{{!-- The chat message itself (CONFIG.ChatMessage.template). Every message in the log is drawn
      here — typed text, an emote, a whisper, a roll, a table draw, a card this system posts — so
      nothing in the log is core's parchment and no card has to be framed after the fact.

      Core's ChatLog finds a message by `li.message[data-message-id]` and refreshes
      `.message-timestamp` in place; those, and the two data-actions, are the only markup it needs
      from here. `borderColor` (the author's colour on an OOC message) is deliberately not drawn:
      it arrives as an inline `style` attribute, which no ordinary declaration can override, and
      the frame is ink.

      The message's `flavor` is the card's caption. Core draws it as a small grey line inside the
      header; here it is the ruled capitals every card head uses, which is why a card posted by
      this system passes its title as `flavor` rather than drawing one of its own. --}}
<li class="chat-message message flexcol cairn2e cairn-message {{cssClass}}" data-message-id="{{message._id}}">
    <header class="message-header flexrow">
        <span class="cairn-message-sender">{{alias}}</span>
        <span class="message-metadata">
            <time class="message-timestamp">{{timeSince message.timestamp}}</time>
            {{#if canDelete}}
            <a aria-label="{{localize 'COMMON.Delete'}}" class="message-delete" data-action="deleteMessage">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-trash" inert></i>
            </a>
            {{/if}}
            {{#if canClose}}
            <a aria-label="{{localize 'CHAT.Dismiss'}}" class="message-dismiss" data-action="dismissMessage">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark" inert></i>
            </a>
            {{/if}}
        </span>
        {{#if isWhisper}}
        <span class="cairn-message-to">{{localize 'CHAT.To'}}: {{whisperTo}}</span>
        {{/if}}
    </header>
    {{#if message.flavor}}
    <div class="cairn-card-title">{{{message.flavor}}}</div>
    {{/if}}
    <div class="message-content cairn-card-body">
        {{{message.content}}}
    </div>
</li>
